  "asr_text": "U.S. roasters keep green beans in stock, then roast and package them. It was also reported that price talks with retailers often happen every three months. There are several steps between the beans and the store shelf. Even when market prices fall, not every step responds with, got it, cut prices now. Of course, around nine months is an estimate from market experts and others. It is not a timer that applies to every company, or a promise that prices will definitely be lower nine months from now. It is too soon to circle a sale on your calendar. In other words, a fall in market prices is not an update button for price tags. The prices on shelves may reflect purchases and talks from some time ago. The next time you see a headline about falling prices, ask the price tag, by the way, how many months ago did you get here?",
